"""
app/workflows/codegen/runner.py
--------------------------------
Entry point for triggering and resuming codegen workflow runs.

Public API
----------
    get_orchestrator()              â†’ singleton compiled graph + checkpointer
    trigger_codegen_run(...)        â†’ seed tasks, create Run, invoke graph
    resume_codegen_run(...)         â†’ resume a paused_hitl run after approval

Run lock
--------
A per-run asyncio.Lock prevents concurrent invocations of the same run_id.
This matters because the LangGraph SQLite checkpointer is not safe for
concurrent writers on the same thread_id.  The lock is process-local â€”
in a multi-worker deployment, Redis-backed distributed locking should
replace it.  A TODO marks that callout.

Checkpointer
------------
AsyncSqliteSaver is created once at first call to get_orchestrator()
and reused for all subsequent calls.  The SQLite DB path comes from
settings.CHECKPOINT_DB_PATH (defaults to "checkpoints/codegen.db").
The directory is created if it doesn't exist.

Task seeding
------------
trigger_codegen_run() reads the architecture run's output_data["tasks"]
(a list of task dicts written by Milestone 4) and creates Task ORM rows
before the graph is invoked.  load_context then reads these rows.

Expected architecture output_data["tasks"] schema
--------------------------------------------------
    [
      {
        "title":       str,
        "description": str,
        "order_index": int,          # optional â€” inferred from list position if absent
        "pattern_refs": list[str],   # optional â€” defaults to []
      },
      ...
    ]

If output_data["tasks"] is absent, trigger_codegen_run raises ValueError
with a clear message â€” codegen cannot proceed without a task list.
"""

